  "title": "A holds message replaces the sender's set, and a replay of it is refused `replayed_counter`",
  "spec": "PROTOCOL.md#137-the-holds-and-their-lease",
  "notes": "A hold is a peer's own statement about itself — the message carries its whole set and no delta, and the peer it belongs to is the key that signed the frame rather than a value in the plaintext — so what the receiver holds afterwards is what `expectHolds` asserts. The replay is the same bytes at the sender's mark, and it is the shape a lease makes necessary: a holder renews unconditionally on its own clock, and a receiver that could not tell a renewal from a replay could not expire a set whose holder had stopped.",
